### Rotating Card (Hover Effect)

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows how to create a card that flips (rotates) when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* 1️⃣  Set up the 3‑D environment */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3‑D effect */
  margin: 50px auto;            /* Center horizontally */
}

/* 2️⃣  The card itself – front + back */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Keep children in 3‑D space */
  transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* Smooth rotation */
}

/* 3️⃣  Front side */
.card .front,
.card .back {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide backside when rotated */
  border-radius: 12px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* 4️⃣  Front styling */
.card .front {
  background: #fff;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #333;
}

/* 5️⃣  Back styling – rotated 180° so it’s hidden initially */
.card .back {
  background: #f8f8f8;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #555;
}

/* 6️⃣  Hover effect – flip the card */
.card-wrapper:hover .card {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1** | `perspective` on the wrapper gives depth to the 3‑D transform. |
| **2** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps child elements in 3‑D space. |
| **3** | `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the backside when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| **4–5** | Front and back sides are positioned absolutely, stacked on top of each other. The back side is pre‑rotated 180° so it’s invisible until the card flips. |
| **6** | On hover, the card rotates 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back side. |

#### Customization tips

- Change `rotateY(180deg)` to `rotateX(180deg)` for a vertical flip.
- Adjust `perspective` value for more or less depth.
- Add `box-shadow`, gradients, images, or any content inside `.front` and `.back`.
- Use media queries to make the card responsive.

Enjoy experimenting with this rotating card!
